        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Prunus tree in blossom,   The base of the tree has been drwan over  an ink study of a stag, which is still visible.  Probably a copy of an original drawing by Ch'en  Lu ( worked first half of the 15th century).\nInscribed with a copy of the artist's tzu Hsien Chang and Su chih yu hui  ( A dark picture of as white original).  Stamped with  collector's seals and those of the artist."@en , "Pap, China, paintings and drawings. Chen Lu (active ca 1440), Hanging scroll flowering plum blossom branch,, ink on silk,"@en ;
